\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Extended Losses Before Fed Minutes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicole Hong and Chiara Albanese   \par \uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2013\par 17:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended their losses Wednesday, hours before the U.S. Federal Reserve was set to release minutes from its most recent policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 Markets from India to Brazil have been battered all week as investors brace for the possibility the Fed will signal greater confidence in the U.S. economy and begin winding down its post-crisis stimulus measures as soon as next month. Emerging markets had been some of the biggest beneficiaries of the easy-money era of the past four years, as near-zero interest rates across the developed world sent investors chasing higher returns elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Local authorities have waged an escalating fight against plunging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Indonesian rupiah's drop this week prompted President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono to promise a package of economic stabilization measures to be unveiled Friday and spurred the country's largest pension funds to boost purchases of Indonesian stocks. The rupiah fell to a new four-year low on Wednesday of 10,914 per dollar, down 5.1% for the week.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee also sank to another record low of 64.52 rupees to the dollar, despite reports that \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Turkish lira fell to a six-week low of 1.9642 lira against the greenback, shrugging off a surprise lending rate hike by \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, which was aimed at fighting the lira's slide. On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would sell at least $100 million daily to support the lira.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold more than $1 billion to prop up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, traders said, after the ringgit dropped to a three-year low. The Brazilian real fell to a four-year low earlier this week, last trading at 2.4143 per dollar, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempted to slow the real's decline with a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions this week.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say they expect Wednesday's Fed minutes to potentially spur more selling of emerging-market assets if they show growing discussions within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over when and how it will taper its stimulus program.\par \par \uc2 "Tapering speculation is gaining momentum, which is weighing on sentiment towards emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Thu Lan Nguyen, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors are particularly concerned about countries like Turkey and India that have current-account deficits, meaning they import more than they export. Once the U.S. begins to pull back on its stimulus, investors fear these emerging economies will struggle to pay for those imports, which could hinder growth.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the South African rand was also under pressure, with the dollar rising to 10.276 rand, the weakest level for the rand since the beginning of July. The Mexican peso fell to a six-week low of 13.148 pesos to the dollar, a day after data showed the Mexican economy contracted in the second quarter for the first time in four years.\par \par \uc2 Write to Nicole Hong at Nicole.Hong@wsj.com and Chiara Albanese at Chiara.Albanese@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 21, 2013 11:04 ET (15:04 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130821e98l004ru\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
