\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 India Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  to Ease Liquidity\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nupur Acharya   \par \uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2013\par 18:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday said it will repurchase government bonds to increase the availability of cash in the banking system, a step that appears to be partial reversal of the slew of measures it took since mid-July to tighten liquidity.\par \par \uc2 In a late evening news release, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  said it will buy back 80 billion rupees ($1.26 billion) of longer-term government bonds Friday. Thereafter, further repurchase will depend on evolving market conditions, it said.\par \par \uc2 It is important to ensure that the liquidity tightening doesn't harden longer-term bond yields and impact the flow of credit to productive sectors of the economy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Since mid-July, the RBI has taken a number of steps to tighten liquidity in the banking system as part of its efforts to stop a free fall in the rupee \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value.\par \par \uc2 On July 15, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  put a limit on the amount of cash banks could borrow at its policy lending rate of 7.25%. It also asked banks to keep aside a portion of their deposits in cash on a daily basis, and started selling short-term cash-management bills to drain liquidity from the system.\par \par \uc2 However, the impact of these steps was short-lived as the rupee continued to fall as investors across Asia braced for a possible withdrawal of the U.S. Federal Reserve's bond-buying program that has increased global liquidity in recent years. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit an all-time low of 64.11 to a dollar on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the cash crunch increased interest rates in the economy as banks raised both deposit and lending rates, further hurting prospects for a recovery in the economy that expanded at a decade-low pace of 5% in the last fiscal year ended March 31.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also relaxed some rules that will help banks deal with the notional, or marked-to-market, loss in their government bond portfolios due to a sharp fall in bond prices, a concern that has been weighing on the shares of banks for the past couple of sessions. They don't have to record their current losses immediately as the RBI has allowed them to spread it over the remaining period of this fiscal year.\par \par \uc2 "These steps have come as a major relief," said Krishnamoorthy Harihar, treasurer at \uc2 FirstRand Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Harihar said he expects these measures to help both foreign investors and local banks to return to the bond market.\par \par \uc2 Write to Nupur Acharya at nupur.acharya@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 20-08-13 1600GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020130820e98k000gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
