\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Indian rupee hits record low before  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  lends support\b0\par\par\uc2 970 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2013\par 05:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee falls to record low of 64.13/dollar\par \par \uc2 * Moderate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market cited by traders\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells $9.3 bln of government bond quotas on Tuesday (Updates close, adds debt limit auction results)\par \par \uc2 By Subhadip Sircar and Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell past 64 to the dollar for the first time on Tuesday and bond yields spiked to a five-year high before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as Asia's third-largest economy bore the brunt of the global emerging markets selloff.\par \par \uc2 Underscoring how hard it is for New Delhi to push through reforms despite the urgency of a deteriorating economic outlook, parliament was adjourned on Tuesday due to protests by members over a corruption scandal.\par \par \uc2 India's notoriously dysfunctional lower house of parliament was due to debate a bill to allow foreign investment in the fledgling private pension industry, a reform seen as key to government efforts to attract investment and narrow the current account deficit, which is exacerbating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis.\par \par \uc2 "India's problems are nowhere near resolution because New Delhi has not done anything - there is no focus on improving productivity, infrastructure or getting FDI (foreign direct investment) back," said Nomura credit analyst Pradeep Mohinani in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 "It's all about stemming the flow of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that is not the cause of the problem," he said.\par \par \uc2 However, India managed to sell $9.3 billion worth of government debt limits to foreign institutional investors, although at rock bottom prices, a sign that they hold out hope of improving market conditions.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners have offloaded $10 billion in Indian debt since May 22, when the U.S. Federal Reserve first signalled its intention to begin scaling back its quantitative easing. They now hold only 43 percent of the $30 billion limit available to them in \uc2 Indian government\uc2  debt.\par \par \uc2 The rupee slumped as much as 1.6 percent to an all-time low 64.13 to the dollar, but recovered most of its losses to close at 63.25/26, down about 0.2 percent on the day, after sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar sales in both the spot and forward markets.\par \par \uc2 Stocks also recovered after hitting near-year lows, with the main share index closing down 0.34 percent. Earlier, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  downgraded Indian equities to "neutral" from "overweight", citing strains in the balance of payments, while Citi cut its Sensex target to 18,900 from 20,800.\par \par \uc2 Bond yields spiked to 9.48 percent, a level not seen since before the \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  crisis in 2008, before stability in the rupee helped them recover. Yields closed down 33 basis points on the day, snapping a five-day rise for their biggest single-day fall since May 2010. ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ GRAPHIC India credit spreads widen as sliding rupee bits\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zec52v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zec52v}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 BORROWING RATES RISING\par \par \uc2 A spate of measures by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government has failed to halt the rupee slide, with liquidity tightening measures aimed at making it harder to short the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushing up borrowing rates and battering corporate and investor sentiment.\par \par \uc2 State-run oil firms, the largest dollar buyers in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, face a deterioration in credit quality if they have to share a higher burden of the country's fuel subsidies due to rising crude prices and a falling rupee, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Srei \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 , an equipment finance company, on Tuesday raised its benchmark lending rate by 50 basis points to 17.75 percent, citing a continued rise in borrowing costs. Several Indian banks have also raised lending rates in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 "Our rate hike has become imperative to maintain the quality of our portfolio," D.K. Vyas, chief executive officer at SREI \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 WEAK GOVERNMENT, WEAK ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister \uc2 Manmohan Singh\uc2 's weak coalition government, heading into national elections by next May, has been hamstrung from pushing through reforms to attract more long-term capital and close a record-high current account gap that has made India vulnerable to flows away from emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Since Singh's government took office for a second term in 2009, the parliament has been the least productive in nearly three decades, according to PRS Legislative Research.\par \par \uc2 Instead, India has been limited to piecemeal measures such as Monday's move to increase the foreign direct investment cap in asset reconstruction companies to 74 percent from 49 percent, and a ban on the duty-free import of flat-screen TVs from Aug. 26.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the RBI simplified rules for investment in shares and debt of Indian companies listed on local exchanges by non-resident Indians.\par \par \uc2 The rupee's plunge also adds to worries about whether Finance Minister P. Chidambaram will be able to meet his goal to pare the fiscal deficit to 4.8 percent of gross domestic product (GDP) this fiscal year.\par \par \uc2 Rating agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  said that while the rupee depreciation was a new variable for the economy, the factors underpinning it have been incorporated in its investment grade rating for India.\par \par \uc2 India is at the lowest investment-grade sovereign rating.\par \par \uc2 "We believe that meeting the fiscal deficit target will be very challenging this year, given lower than anticipated growth holding back revenue growth and steep rupee depreciation raising the subsidy bill on imported goods," analyst Atsi Sheth said in an e-mailed reply to queries from Reuters. (Additional reporting by Umesh Desai in HONG KONG, Archana Narayanan, Neha Dasgupta, Suvashree Dey Choudhury and Abhishek Vishnoi in MUMBAI, and Frank Jack Daniel in NEW DELHI; Editing by Tony Munroe & Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 3) | ABN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | D | M | O | OIL | ABX | BNX | FUN | SNI | SNS | DNP | PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130823e98k0003y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
