\par\par \b \uc2 India cbank helps rupee recover after hitting life low\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2013\par 14:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends at 60.77/78 per dlr versus 60.88/89 on Monday\par \par \uc2 * INR hits life low of 61.80; cbank steps in to sell dlrs\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2 's appointment as RBI chief also cheers mkt\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 6 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee hit a record low of 61.80 on Tuesday but recovered after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the appointment of \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  as the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor raised hopes of a new approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said heavy dollar demand from importers throughout the day had pressured the rupee before the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped it recover and post a 0.2 percent gain for the day.\par \par \uc2 Media reports the government was gearing up to announce new measures to attract foreign inflows, including potentially raising debt via state-run companies and banks, also helped the rupee recover.\par \par \uc2 New measures could reduce the pressure somewhat on the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  to announce new cash-draining measures to prop up the rupee, just as India has announced chief economic adviser \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  would lead the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  when Duvvuri Subbarao's tenure as governor ends in September.\par \par \uc2 "Rajan's appointment is positive news. But I am not expecting any major shift in RBI policy given the constraints it has to face on macro and micro levels," said \uc2 Pramod Patil\uc2 , assistant vice president, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets at \uc2 United Overseas Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Even though there was good dollar selling by state-run banks today, I feel the rupee will test 62 levels towards the weekend unless RBI takes some concrete action," he added.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed at 60.77/78 per dollar compared with 60.88/89 on Monday. The unit moved in a wide band of 60.75 to 61.80 during the session.\par \par \uc2 Traders said good arbitrage opportunities between the onshore and offshore forward markets were also a reason for the rupee's fall.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has fallen 1.5 percent since the RBI unveiled measures to drain cash on July 15, raising doubts about the efficacy of the measures, especially as increased government spending has kept liquidity easy and not tight.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the government would ultimately need to take meaningful steps to address the record high current account deficit and stem further declines in the rupee.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore non-deliverable forwards, the one-month contract was at 61.46 while the three-month was at 62.40.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar/rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all closed at around 61.47 with a total traded volume of $3.3 billion. (Editing by Anupama Dwivedi)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / | ABN | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130809e986000iq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
