\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee gains on rumoured cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 ; second week of win\b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2013\par 14:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends at 59.35/36 vs 59.67/68 Thursday close * PM Singh says RBI can withdraw measures if short-term pressures ease\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Short positions in INR increase - Reuters poll\par     By Subhadip Sircar\par     MUMBAI, July 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee gained on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumoured \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the session to support a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had floundered and been on the verge of wiping out all gains since policymakers' measures to drain liquidity. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained 0.3 percent for the week, marking its second consecutive weekly gain, even as traders said the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's measures to raise short-term interest rates to support the rupee unveiled late on Monday have not yet had a meaningful impact. Concerns have risen about the success of the steps after the government cancelled a treasury bill sale and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to reject most bids at a special bond sale as investors demanded higher yields. At least the rupee drew some solace from Prime Minister \uc2 Manmohan Singh\uc2 's comments that the RBI can withdraw measures once short term pressures ease. "RBI will clearly not give up the vigil. They are trying to achieve a balance between demand and supply," said Satyajit Kanjilal, chief executive at ForexServe. He said the rupee has a key resistance at 58.80 to the dollar which, if breached, may see a move to 57.30 levels. The partially convertible rupee ended at 59.35/36 per dollar, against its previous close of 59.67/68. For the week, it ended 0.3 percent higher. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have adopted a pattern of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late trades in recent sessions, dealers said. "Maximum impact with minimum effort," a dealer summed it up. Bond yields posted their worst week in four-and-a-half years with yields rising 40 basis points, roiled by the RBI's steps. Short positions in the rupee increased during the past two weeks despite authorities' steps to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Reuters poll showed. In the offshore non-deliverable forwards, the one-month contract was at 59.76 while the three-month was at 60.58. In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar/rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all closed around 59.53 with a total traded volume of $2 billion. (Editing by Jijo Jacob)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ | ABN | D | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130722e97j000jb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
