\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  RBI Subbarao: Exchange Rate Largely Market-Driven,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  to Curb Volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2013\par 06:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 18 Jul 2013 01:27 EDT DJ  RBI Subbarao: Rupee Exchange Rate Largely Market-Driven\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Sudeep Jain \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI--India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor reiterated that the rupee exchange rate is largely market-determined and that the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to dampen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility and preserve macroeconomic stability.\par \par \uc2 The comments were part of a speech Wednesday delivered by Duvvuri Subbarao in London, a copy of which was released on the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's website Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has been hit hard by the capital flight from emerging markets due to expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will wind down its bond buying program that has kept global markets flush with liquidity in recent years. The local unit has fallen 10.0% against the U.S. dollar since May and hit a record low of 61.21 to the U.S. dollar on July 8. It was changing hands at 59.73 to the dollar in early trade on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to prop up the rupee, possibly because \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $280 billion are not enough to cover even seven months worth of imports, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this week tightened liquidity in the local banking system to make it harder for traders to buy dollars with borrowed rupees.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sudeep Jain at sudeep.jain@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 18, 2013 01:27 ET (05:27 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130718e97i00192\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
