\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Buoying Rupee Leaves India In Bind\b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2013\par 00:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par C3\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (FROM THE WALL STREET JOURNAL 7/17/13) \par    By Sudeep Jain \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is walking a tightrope -- trying to arrest the rupee's sharp decline as global capital flows out, without raising interest rates in a way that could slam growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 India's economy is growing at its slowest pace in a decade, and higher rates could choke off an acceleration expected later this year. On the flip side, policy makers are unnerved by a record-breaking slide in the rupee that threatens to pump up import prices.\par \par \uc2 Late Monday, following sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tighter trading rules, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  set a limit on the amount banks can borrow from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the benchmark interest rate of 7.25%. Above that limit, banks would have to pay much higher interest.\par \par \uc2 The RBI also said it would sell 120 billion rupees ($2 billion) of bonds Thursday, on top of a scheduled 150 billion-rupee bond sale Friday, in an effort to drain funds from the banking system.\par \par \uc2 The efforts helped the rupee pick up to its highest point in two weeks. But economists fear these steps could end up hurting the rupee if foreign investors conclude economic growth will suffer, and sell Indian assets.\par \par \uc2 "They are trying to do the right thing, trying to make it expensive to [sell] the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but there can be a cost to pay in terms of growth," said Bhanu Baweja, a \uc2 UBS\b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst in London.\par \par \uc2 In the short term, investors bought the rupee, pushing the dollar down to 59.17 rupees, analysts said. In late trading in New York on Monday, the dollar was at 59.32 rupees. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had a tough run. The dollar rose to 61.21 rupees on July 8, and the rupee and is down 9% against the greenback this year, making it one of the worst performers in Asia. India depends heavily on imports for commodities such as crude oil, so a weak rupee stokes inflation.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will soon begin winding down a bond-buying program has prompted outflows from most emerging markets in recent months.\par \par \uc2 With India dependent on foreign money to fund its current-account gap-- which reached a record 4.8% of gross domestic product in the year ended March 31-- the recent outflows from emerging markets have hit the rupee especially hard.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  associated with current-account deficits will be at the mercy of global capital flows," said Siddharth Mathur, head of Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and local markets strategy at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's efforts mirror steps by other governments to protect their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by tightening monetary policy. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Indonesia\uc2  raised its benchmark rate and a key money-market rate by half a percentage point last week, sacrificing growth prospects in an effort to protect the rupiah. \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it might raise rates as soon as next week, while Brazil has boosted rates three times this year.\par \par \uc2 "We have to expect more efforts from emerging-market central banks to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Murat Toprak, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 The RBI raised rates by 3.75 percentage points between March 2010 and October 2011 to tame inflation. Since April 2012 it has cut rates by 1.25 percentage points to support growth.\par \par \uc2 High interest rates, a weak external environment and a large fiscal deficit have taken a toll on India. The economy grew 5% in the year ended March 31, well off its 9% pace two years ago.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Katie Martin and Chiara Albanese contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 16, 2013 18:30 ET (22:30 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130716e97g0054c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
