\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ Blog:Top India Stories From WSJ: Joint Power Grid With Pakistan Discussed, RBI Seen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  to Help Rupee, Gold, Silver Imports Fall\b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2013\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's India Real Time Report blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/indiarealtime/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/indiarealtime/  }}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Your daily round-up of the best of Wall Street Journal's India coverage:\par \par \uc2 India, Pakistan Discuss Joint Power Grid: India has warmed up to arch-rival Pakistan by offering to help its neighbor resolve an acute power shortage that has plunged its cities in hours of darkness and blighted economic growth, two senior government officials confirmed Friday.\par \par \uc2 RBI Seen \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Help Rupee: \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely sold U.S. dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday afternoon to support the rupee, three dealers said.\par \par \uc2 India's Gold, Silver Imports Fall: India's gold and silver imports in June fell 70% from the previous month following steps taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the federal government to curb demand, a senior government official said Friday.\par \par \uc2 Congress Party Confident on Food Law: India's government is confident that Parliament will validate this week's executive order to launch a food aid program, a senior official of the party that leads the ruling coalition said Friday.\par \par \uc2 India Farmers Step Up Sowing: Farmers in India planted summer crops on nearly double the area until Friday compared with last year as monsoon rains covered the country in record time, brightening prospects for a bumper output.\par \par \uc2 Unilever\uc2  to Raise Stake in Indian Unit: \uc2 Unilever PLC\uc2  will spend $3.2 billion to increase its stake in its Indian unit \uc2 Hindustan Unilever Ltd\uc2 . by 14.8%, the company said late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Adani Group\uc2 's $1.65 Billion \uc2 Indonesian Railway\uc2  Project Collapses : \uc2 Adani Group\uc2  has pulled out of a $1.65 billion Indonesian railway project with state-controlled coal miner PT Bukit Asam after the Indian conglomerate was confronted by rising costs and permit issues, Bukit Asam's chief executive said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at   \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com  }}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 06-07-13 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130706e9760000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
