\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 India Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Seen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Market\b0\par\par\uc2 By Khushita Vasant \par \uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2013\par 12:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely sold U.S. dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday afternoon to support the rupee, three dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  likely sold dollars through state-owned banks after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  threatened to touch a new record high, the dealers said.\par \par \uc2 A handful of state-run banks were spotted selling dollars around 60.55 rupees, pointing to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity in the market, the dealers said. The dollar soon eased to 60.40 rupees and was last at 60.47 rupees.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to as high as 60.58 rupees during the day. It had hit a record high of 60.75 rupees last week.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on its presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. It has stated before that it only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to reduce volatility and doesn't defend any particular level for the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has lost more than 11% of its value against the dollar since the start of May, making it one of the worst-performing emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 Friday, the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as investors anticipate the U.S. jobless rate may fall in June. The jobs report is due at 1230 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Conditions in the U.S. labor market are being seen as the key determinant of the Federal Reserve's policy toward the withdrawal from its $85 billion-a-month bond-buying program. Foreign investors are pulling money out of emerging markets like India and investing in dollar-denominated assets which now appear more attractive.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, worries over India's large current-account deficit and sluggish economic growth have made foreign investors to withdraw money from the country's markets, weakening the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Khushita Vasant at khushita.vasant@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 05-07-13 1009GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020130705e975000d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
