\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee closes in on record lows; cbank fears cap losses\b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2013\par 13:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends 59.68/69 per dlr versus 59.27/28 on Friday\par \par \uc2 * Fears of RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeping INR losses capped - dealers\par \par \uc2 * RBI, govt taking steps on economy- RBI deputy\par \par \uc2 By Subhadip Sircar\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell to near record lows on Monday as foreign investors continue to sell debt and stocks as part of an exit from emerging markets, with only fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  arresting a further drop.\par \par \uc2 The rupee is likely to continue hovering around a record low of 59.9850 hit on Thursday as long as global markets remain weak over worries about the rollback of U.S. monetary stimulus and concerns about China's financial sector.\par \par \uc2 Dealers were split about whether the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot and onshore forward markets, suggesting any action would not have been strong. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen likely to defend the 60 level for the rupee, which also provides formidable technical and psychological resistance.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of India Deputy Governor \uc2 Anand Sinha\uc2  said on Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 Indian government\uc2  are doing whatever is needed to get a "hold over" the deteriorating macro economic conditions.\par \par \uc2 Investors are now awaiting the release of the current account deficit data on Friday, which will underline whether the funding pressures for the economy will further rise.\par \par \uc2 "One key factor is whether foreign equity investors pull out. But the government and RBI look determined to take steps to stem the rupee's fall," said Samir Lodha, senior partner at QuantArt.\par \par \uc2 "The RBI seems to have been active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the past few sessions. They seem to be protecting the 60 level for now."\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed at 59.68/69 per dollar, against its previous close of 59.27/28. It fell to a low of 59.8250 in session.\par \par \uc2 India's BSE index shed 1.2 percent on continued worries about outflows after foreign institutional investors sold cash shares for nine straight sessions, totalling 77.60 billion rupees ($1.31 billion), as per exchange and regulatory data.\par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have sold a net $5.33 billion in rupee debt since May 22, the day Fed Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  first hinted at stimulus withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore non-deliverable forwards, the one-month contract was at 60.14, while the three-month was at 60.84.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar/rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all closed around 59.79 with a total traded volume of $6.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Anupama Dwivedi)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / | ABN | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130627e96o000kl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
