\par\par \b \uc2 DJ India Official:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Supporting Rupee at INR60 to a Dollar Level\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prasanta Sahu  \par \uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2013\par 09:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the U.S. dollar below 60 rupees, a senior official from \uc2 India's finance ministry\uc2  said Friday, spelling out a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  target of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the rupee trades near a record low.\par \par \uc2 "Sixty is a psychological barrier which the government and RBI [\uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 ] don't want to be breached," the official, who didn't want to be named, told The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 The comments sent the rupee to its day's high of 59.21 to the dollar in early afternoon trade, dealers said. The local unit had been quoted at 59.57 in late Asian trade Thursday, after hitting a record low of 59.93 earlier in the session.\par \par \uc2 The official didn't specify whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, but dealers said it's unlikely.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on at least two separate occasions, dealers had said.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's spokeswoman wasn't immediately available for comment.\par \par \uc2 The RBI says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets only to curb volatility and not to target a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. The rupee is one of Asia's worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year and has lost more than 9.0% against the dollar since the start of May.\par \par \uc2 While most emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been hurt by expectations that the U.S. will taper its monetary stimulus, the rupee has been hit particularly hard due to India's large current account deficit. The current account gap was a record 6.7% of gross domestic product in the October-December quarter, according to the latest data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The official also said the government would take steps to encourage stable capital flows into India, without elaborating.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prasanta Sahu at prasanta.sahu@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 21-06-13 0752GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020130621e96l000bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
