\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indian officials pour balm over troubled rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2013\par 10:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee rebounds from record low hit on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 * Policy adviser says cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 * Econ affairs secretary says govt considering measures (Updates with quotes, details, background)\par \par \uc2 By Neha Dasgupta and Suvashree Dey Choudhury\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 12 (Reuters) - India said on Wednesday it was considering measures that would help stabilise the rupee after it hit an all-time low but the assurances are unlikely to be enough unless backed by concrete steps to revive inflows into the slowing economy.\par \par \uc2 The government may issue an overseas bond to raise capital for infrastructure, economic affairs secretary \uc2 Arvind Mayaram\uc2  said a day after another official said the government may target overseas Indians for a debt issue.\par \par \uc2 Mayaram, however, said the government had no plans to moderate gold imports which have been a key reason for a large current account deficit that is putting pressure on the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The rupee rebounded on Wednesday to trade at 58.00/01 per dollar from Tuesday's record low of 58.98 but trimmed gains after a higher-than-expected consumer price inflation reading for May.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit the buffers the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the deputy chairman of the Planning Commission Montek Singh Ahluwalia said, confirming suspicions that the rupee rebounded from RBI dollar sales.\par \par \uc2 The RBI late on Tuesday also asked exporters at special economic zones to realise their dollar earnings and get them back into the country within one year in a bid to increase the supply of dollars in the market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also hastened the process of dollar inflows through online payment channels by increasing the amount that exporters can bring back to $10,000 from $3000.\par \par \uc2 "The government talking up the rupee has had an impact on the sentiment. Going ahead, if the macros remain weak, the government will have to take steps to further attract inflows," said Anjali Verma, economist at PhilipCapital in Mumbai.\par \par \uc2 SELLOFF IN EMERGING MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The downward pressure on Indian assets has been exacerbated by the recent selloff across emerging markets and Indian officials have pointed to a broad rally in the dollar as the trigger for the latest falls.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has fallen more than 8 percent since the beginning of May, and although that is the worst performance in Asia, other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also being hit.\par \par \uc2 "We'll keep looking at different instruments, and bonds are one of the instruments we are looking at for raising resources for long-term infrastructure financing," said Mayaram on the sidelines of a conference in Mumbai on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers are also trying to comfort investors by focusing on measures to help narrow the current account deficit, including easing foreign direct investment rules.\par \par \uc2 Tackling India's current account deficit, which hit a record 6.7 percent of gross domestic product in October-December, is seen as key to preventing continued weakness in the rupee.\par \par \uc2 "It will be a totality of our efforts to convey the impression that the current account deficit is being brought under control and the economy is going to rebound," Ahluwalia told CNBC-TV 18 in an interview.\par \par \uc2 For now, the rupee is likely to remain dependant on global movements of the dollar, ahead of key data this week including wholesale inflation and trade data and the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy review on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "They (RBI) did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday which would suggest that they felt market pressures were pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an unnecessary low point," said Ahluwalia. (Additional reporting by Subhadip Sircar and Swati Bhat; Editing by Rafael Nam and Sanjeev Miglani)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-POLICY/ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130612e96c000ar\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
