\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,146 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2013\par 02:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range Larger Range \par  \par  \par    USD/CNY       -             - \par    USD/TWD       -             - \par    USD/KRW  1,123-1,130   1,120-1,137 \f28 \par \par \uc2 USD/SGD 1.2533-1.2572 1.2504-1.2600\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR 3.1200-3.1500 3.1145-3.1550\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/THB  30.50-30.94   30.40-31.00 \par    USD/PHP       -             - \par    USD/IDR  9,770-9,800   9,720-9,820 \par    USD/INR  58.00-58.50   57.50-59.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/CNY - markets are closed for a holiday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD - markets are closed for a holiday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW - consolidation. USD/KRW is slipping out of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel as the WSJ Dollar Index slides due to USD/JPY's steep overnight fall and the euro's rise. The USD/KRW pair may step into a slightly lower range of 1,123-1,130, supported by the 20-day Bollinger mid and capped by the Bollinger uptrend channel cum psychological resistance at 1,130. There could be more capitulation of long-USD positions before the market can trade higher again. If the pair ends the day above 1,130, there might be another attempt to re-test the 2013 high of 1,145.3. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is 1,123 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1,120 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,130 (psychological resistance and Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,137 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,140 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD - consolidation. USD/SGD may slip a tad before consolidating at the Bollinger downtrend channel entrance at 1.2504. The overnight dip in the WSJ Dollar Index, mainly due to dollar/yen sliding under Y96.00 and the euro rallying past $1.3300, may keep a lid on USD/SGD Wednesday. Though a tone of risk aversion is still hovering in emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Singapore dollar has a regional safe-haven status that will help it to hold on to its value better than some of its peers. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2533 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2504 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2572 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1.2600 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and psychological resistance), before 1.2640 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR - intraday lower, mid-term upside bias. USD/MYR may have found an interim ceiling at the top of the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.1550 and could now retreat toward the 3.1200 psychological support as the WSJ Dollar Index slides. The USD/MYR pair however will maintain its mid-term upside bias as long as it ends the day above the 3.1000 base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, which is also a major psychological barrier. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is 3.1200 (psychological support), then at 3.1145 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1000 (psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.1500 (psychological resistance), before 3.1550 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB - consolidation. USD/THB has reached its short-term target of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 30.94 and is likely to stabilize under the 31.00 psychological barrier for now. Weakness in the WSJ Dollar index, mostly due to the steep overnight fall in USD/JPY, is likely to be a drag on USD/THB. However, if the USD/THB pair manages to climb above the 31.06 top of the weekly Cloud resistance zone, more gains are likely sooner. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.50 (psychological support), then at 30.40 (weekly Bollinger mid support), before 30.23 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 30.94 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 31.00 (psychological resistance), before 31.06 (top of weekly Cloud resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP - markets are closed for a holiday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR - consolidation. Spot USD/IDR will likely be stable once again due to suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capping the pair around 9.810-9,820 and a slightly softer greenback all around. The USD/IDR NDF market is experiencing a pullback from its 4-year high, though the 1-month NDF contract still trades above the psychological barrier of 10,000. Tuesday saw the 1-month NDF contract, the most liquid one in the NDF market, trade at a 4-year high of 10,405. Traders will be watching for signs of normalization in the 1-month NDF premium - the price difference over the standard spot contract - before resuming confidence in the rupiah. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 9,770 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 9,740 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 9,720 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 9,800 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 9,810 (suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), before 9,820 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR - intraday lower, mid-term upside bias. USD/INR could drop further Wednesday as long-USD positions take profit, spooked by direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling dollars just before the 59.00 barrier to support the rupee late Tuesday. The pair could retreat to the psychological support at 57.50 if stoploss orders below the 58.00 barrier are triggered. Some analysts are calling for the rupee to gain from here as the fundamentals for the Indian economy could improve soon, due to falling inflation and the government's attempts to reduce gold demand in order to deal with the current account deficit. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 58.00 (psychological support), then at 57.50 (top of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological support), before 57.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 58.50 (psychological resistance), then at 59.00 (major psychological resistance and RBI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 12-06-13 0047GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130612e96c0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
