\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cbank seen  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  markets to support rupee-dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2013\par 10:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee recovered sharply from record lows on Tuesday afternoon, as three dealers cited dollar sales by state-run banks on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, they said the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not seem too large, with the steep recovery in the rupee being exaggerated by illiquid conditions in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee was trading at 58.47/48 per dollar at 2:04 p.m. (0834 GMT), off a record low of 58.98 hit earlier in the day, but still weaker than its close of 58.15/16 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the rupee was also supported by speculation that May wholesale inflation due this week may show continued easing and media reports the government was considering a special bond sale for non-resident Indians. (Reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RUPEE/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT) | ABN | D | M | SNI | SNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130614e96b000bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
