\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-RBI's hidden hand pulls Indian rupee off record low\b0\par\par\uc2 760 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2013\par 05:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee hits life low of 58.98 to the dollar, ends at 58.39/40\par \par \uc2 * Cbank likely sold dlrs via state-run banks, say dealers\par \par \uc2 * Comments from chief econ advisor to the govt also aid sentiment (Updates close, adds economic advisor's comments, NDF market movements)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 11 (Reuters) - Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hauled the rupee off a record low struck on Tuesday afternoon, reassuring a market worried by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's earlier inaction as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall gathered pace.\par \par \uc2 Striking 58.98 per dollar at its weakest, the rupee had plunged 3.25 percent this week, notching record lows for two consecutive days.\par \par \uc2 Dollar-selling by state banks, believed to be acting at the behest of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prevented a fall though the 59 per dollar level, though intermittent bouts of dollar selling by exporters had also slowed the fall.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee recovered to close at 58.39/40 per dollar, but it was still 0.4 percent weaker than Monday's close of 58.15/16.\par \par \uc2 "Finally the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in. The selling was not huge, but enough to cause a rebound in the rupee," said a senior dealer with a state-run bank, who declined to be identified given the sensitivity of the matter.\par \par \uc2 Comments from senior government officials had offered little comfort to investors until stronger comments came on Tuesday, immediately following the talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the securities markets regulator will take "warranted" action to stall a sharp fall in the rupee, the Finance Ministry's chief economic adviser \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He also added that oil companies had agreed to stagger dollar purchases as much as possible to reduce pressure on the rupee, which would mark an important move, considering these firms are the biggest domestic buyers of the greenback.\par \par \uc2 However, the market continues to remain jittery.\par \par \uc2 "The rupee has rebounded today, but the market continues to remain nervous," said Vikas Babu Chittiprolu, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with state-run \uc2 Andhra Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There is not much exporter selling even now. I expect 57.70 to 59.30 range for the rest of the week," he added.\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had intensified after comments on the limitations of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Duvvuri Subbarao on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Subbarao said a failed defence of rupee can be worse than no defence, and reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market only to manage volatility.\par \par \uc2 "Fundamentally, INR will continue to depreciate because of CAD (current account deficit), but this move has happened too soon and too fast," said Samir Lodha, managing director at QuantArt Market Solutions.\par \par \uc2 Analysts noted that while foreign institutional investors (FIIS) were still net buyers of debt and equity so far in 2013, the risk that they could turn sellers could force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to at least moderate the volatility.\par \par \uc2 "Technically, the rupee has made a short term low of 58.98 levels, from these levels, we expect a correction till 57.50-57.25 levels but the overall view still remains bearish," said Abhishek Goenka, chief executive at India \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Advisors.\par \par \uc2 The weakness in the rupee has prompted investors to exit their positions in the debt market while the domestic equity market is also under selling pressure.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has dropped in 16 of the last 18 trading sessions and is down 7.9 percent since the start of May. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been the worst performer in Asia since the start of May.\par \par \uc2 The fall in the spot rupee was also exacerbated by the large long dollar positions being built in the offshore non-deliverable forwards market, traders said. Indian rupee NDFs were pricing the rupee at 61.89 in a year's time, 5.7 percent weaker than the spot rate of 58.39.\par \par \uc2 "Any respite for the INR from some possible bunched up FII debt and FDI inflows this month will be temporary," said Rajeev Malik, senior economist at CLSA in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "Barring volatility, the INR will eventually weaken to cross 60/USD in a sustained manner. Admittedly, this is playing out sooner than we expected because of the earlier change in the global backdrop," he added. (Reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Tony Munroe/Simon Cameron-Moore)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/OPEN (UPDATE 3) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | SNI | SNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130614e96b0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
