\par\par \b \uc2 Selloff in Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Accelerates as \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Yields Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 1,115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2013\par 14:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunge as selloff accelerates\par \par \uc2 --Yen rises sharply as demand for perceived safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  soars\par \par \uc2 --South African rand at fresh four-year low against dollar\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after rupee falls to record low\par \par \uc2 --Turkish lira bucks the trend as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells dollars at three separate auctions\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Clare Connaghan \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under intense selling pressure Tuesday, with the Indian rupee slumping to a fresh record low and the South African rand falling to a new four-year low against the dollar, as fresh expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve will unwind its monetary stimulus in the coming months pushed up \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rand once again felt the brunt of the selloff, losing more than 1% in European trading hours, as the dollar rose to as high as ZAR10.3610 at one point, marking the South African \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakest level since mid-March 2009. The Mexican peso also felt the pain, slumping to its weakest level this year, as a jump in U.S. 10-year Treasury yields to a 14-month high drove traders and investors away from emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The widening in \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields has triggered a sharp repricing among emerging market assets," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The drop in Treasury bond prices lacked a clear immediate trigger. But upbeat labor-market data Friday, the move by ratings firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  to upgrade its outlook on the U.S. Monday, combined with a fresh reminder by Fed official \f28 \uc2 \f2 James Bullard\f28 \uc2 \f2  that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is watching economic data carefully to pick its time to change policy, all contributed to the decline. In addition, $66 billion of new Treasury bonds are due to hit the market this week. Typically, investors sell older bonds to make space for new debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The plunge in emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday is nothing new as these markets have experienced bouts of heavy selling pressure ever since U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ben Bernanke\f28 \uc2 \f2  and minutes from a recent Fed policy meeting in May suggested the Fed might start pulling back on its bond purchases some time this year. That made investors fear that the tide of money flowing into emerging markets might soon diminish.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The selloff has been so severe in some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that it has prompted action from authorities, with Brazil and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past week to support their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is suspected of joining that club Tuesday, with local dealers reporting the bank sold U.S. dollars in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to support the battered rupee, after the dollar pushed as high as INR58.98.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Only the Turkish lira managed to buck the overall trend, stabilizing after an early dive, but only because the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warned it would start additional short-term monetary tightening if needed to stabilize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . As protests in the country continued Tuesday, the lira fell to TRY1.9098, its weakest level against the buck since December 2011. However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rebounded when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made its announcement and then subsequently conducted three separate dollar sales of $50 million each.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Outside emerging markets, the dollar's performance was mixed against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rising sharply against the commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Australia, New Zealand and Canada, while falling against the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar fell below $0.9350 against the greenback for the first time since September 2010, while the New Zealand dollar slumped to a one-year low against the buck.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Like emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the so-called commodity-bloc has come under pressure because of concerns the Fed will reel in its bond purchases, while the slowdown in China has also weighed on sentiment. Also, there's less liquidity in these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , so when investors "rush for the exits, the move is more pronounced," said Daragh Maher, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen and Swiss franc were the other big movers in Tuesday's trading session as demand for perceived safe-haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose. Disappointment from the lack of extra action by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  overnight also contributed to the move, participants said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "For the market, we're in a situation where we need something new to feed this yen bear market and when you don't get it and you've got a market positioned for yen weakness, you get pullback's like this," said Mr. Maher.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, news is awaited from the German Constitutional Court hearing in Karlsruhe, which is expected to rule on a complaint about the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's as-yet unused outright monetary transaction bond-buying program. They will also keep a close eye on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1153 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.3283 against the dollar, compared with $1.3258, late Monday in New York, according to trading system EBS. The dollar was at Y96.98 against the yen, compared with Y98.76, while the euro was at Y128.845, compared with Y130.92. The pound was trading at $1.5546 against the dollar, compared with $1.5570 late Monday in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 73.45 from 73.717.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below:\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1040 GMT     1.3285     96.99      1.5550     0.9275 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish    Bullish    Bullish    Range \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Bearish    Bullish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.3033     91.58      1.5551     0.9392 \par 3rd Resistance    1.3434     99.05      1.5782     0.9418 \par 2nd Resistance    1.3325     98.50      1.5684     0.9360 \par 1st Resistance    1.3306     97.80      1.5601     0.9349 \par Pivot*            1.3235     98.49      1.5550     0.9358 \par 1st Support       1.3244     96.48      1.5530     0.9263 \par 2nd Support       1.3219     96.00      1.5490     0.9249 \par 3rd Support       1.3177     94.97      1.5467     0.9225 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       AUD/USD \par  \par Spot 1040 GMT     0.9335 \par 3 Day Trend       Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.0228 \par 3rd Resistance    0.9482 \par 2nd Resistance    0.9455 \par 1st Resistance    0.9403 \par Pivot*            0.9467 \par 1st Support       0.9331 \par 2nd Support       0.9319 \par 3rd Support       0.9240 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Jessica Mead and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Technical\f28 \uc2 \f2  Strategist Francis Bray contributed to this story.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Clare Connaghan at clare.connaghan@dowjones.com [ 06-11-13 0823ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1034 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4162 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020130611e96b0002j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
