\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indian rupee recovers from near 1-yr low; cbank watched\b0\par\par\uc2 643 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2013\par 11:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee ends at 56.84/85 per dlr vs 56.7250/7350 on Wed\par \par \uc2 * Some stability seen as chances of cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise\par \par \uc2 * Rupee seen trading in 56.70-57.10 range on Friday-traders\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 6 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee recovered after touching the key psychological level of 57 to the dollar on Thursday, helped by dollar selling by some foreign and custodian banks, but sentiment remains cautious ahead of key U.S. data on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The initial fall pushed the rupee frighteningly close to a record low hit nearly a year earlier as fears of an end to the U.S. Federal Reserve's monetary stimulus sent the dollar higher.\par \par \uc2 Recent U.S. economic data has been mixed, which has left investors caught between fears the Fed will reduce its stimulus and worries the U.S. economy is still weak.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. data has been weak past few times and if that continues tomorrow, expectations of Fed withdrawing the stimulus will be hampered," said \uc2 Pramod Patil\uc2 , assistant vice-president, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets, at \uc2 United Overseas Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupee is not far off the record low of 57.32 hit in late June last year, raising the prospect of a potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although most analysts do not expect bold actions given that the rupee weakness is tracking global factors.\par \par \uc2 Still, further falls are bound to revive concerns about funding India's current account deficit. The government on Wednesday increased import duty on gold, and the finance ministry is looking at raising the cap on foreign investment in sovereign debt.\par \par \uc2 "The psychological level of 57 has been hit and thus it invites fears of some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The market is a bit cautious at these levels," said Paresh Nayar, head of fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at First Rand Bank.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee closed at 56.84/85 per dollar, after earlier touching 57, its weakest since June 28, 2012. The rupee had closed at 56.7250/7350 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Domestic shares fell on worries about the Fed stimulus programme, tracking Asian indexes that slipped to new 2013 lows. The benchmark BSE index closed down 0.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 Traders also cited heavy dollar demand from oil refiners, the largest buyers of the greenback in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in early trade but dollar selling by foreign and custodian banks helped the unit recover.\par \par \uc2 Comments from a senior government official hurt the rupee as well. Propping up the rupee "artificially" is not the right thing to do, said Montek Singh Ahluwalia, the deputy chairman of the country's Planning Commision.\par \par \uc2 The rupee is expected to hold in a 56.70-57.10 range until the U.S. non-farm payroll data, traders said. The data is due after India market close on Friday and the reaction would be seen on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Domestically, investors are expected to focus on inflation, trade, and industrial output data, all of which are expected ahead of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's policy review on June 17.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cut interest rates a fourth time this year have been recently dashed after Governor Duvvuri Subbarao expressed concern over retail inflation and the current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore non-deliverable forwards, the one-month contract was at 57.20, while the three-month was at 57.78.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar/rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all closed around 56.99 with a total traded volume of $5.3 billion. (Editing by Prateek Chatterjee and Jijo Jacob)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1) | ABN | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130609e9660003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
