\par\par \b \uc2 India's cbank net sold $50 mln in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mkt in June\b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2012\par 13:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 10 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 sold only a net $50 million in June, compared with $485 million in the previous month, data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The RBI sold $700 million in June, while it bought $650 million, marking its smallest net \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a month at least since April 2011, the data showed.\par \par \uc2 The rupee had staged a sharp recovery towards end-June after touching a life-low of 57.32 a dollar on June 22.\par \par \uc2 At 4.30 p.m. (1100 GMT) the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was changing hands at 55.30/31 to a dollar in the secondary market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rolled over forward dollar contracts by purchasing $810 million in June, the data showed.\par \par \uc2 In the forward dollar market, outstanding dollar sales rose to $14.08 billion in June from $10.31 billion in May, RBI data showed, indicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's preference to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward markets to prevent the rupee liquidity from tightening further in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Neha Dasgupta and Swati Bhat; Editing by Jijo Jacob)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RBI/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120810e88a000m3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
