\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: India  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves Fall on Suspected RBI Action\b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2012\par 14:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Reserves down by $2.37 billion to $287.62 billion in week to July 6\par \par \uc2 -- Analyst says RBI may have supplied dollars to oil companies\par \par \uc2 (Recasts; adds analyst's comment in 4th and 9th paragraphs.)\par \par \uc2 By Sudeep Jain\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI--India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell sharply in the week to July 6, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Friday, magnifying concerns over the sufficiency of the reserves amid the recent fall in the Indian rupee.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by $2.37 billion to $287.62 billion in the week ended July 6, mainly due to a $2.3 billion drop in foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a press statement.\par \par \uc2 But, direct \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market may not have been the cause for the fall in reserves, said analysts.\par \par \uc2 The RBI may have supplied foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to state-owned oil refiners to pay for crude-oil imports, said Moses Harding, senior vice president at \uc2 IndusInd Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last month, oil importers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had asked them to route half their dollar purchases through a single state-run bank.\par \par \uc2 This was seen as a move that would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to supply dollars to oil companies when required and isolate a key source of dollar demand from the broad market to reduce the pressure on the Indian rupee.\par \par \uc2 The rupee hit a record low of 57.22 to the dollar on June 22 as investors fled risk-sensitive assets amid the deepening sovereign debt crisis in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has borne the brunt of global risk aversion due to concerns over India's large current-account and fiscal deficits and the government's failure to boost investment. The dollar was quoted at 55.14 rupees late Friday in Asia.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's recent rally against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to rising concerns over global growth may have also reduced the value of the non-dollar assets in India's reserves, Mr. Harding said.\par \par \uc2 The RBI doesn't provide any reasons for the changes in foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets. It also doesn't say whether it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's precarious external position is seen as a key risk for the economy, which is facing the combination of a sharp slowdown and high inflation.\par \par \uc2 The current-account deficit widened to 4.2% of gross domestic product in the fiscal year that ended March 31, after remaining below 3% since 1991, as exports slowed while imports remained high.\par \par \uc2 India's dwindling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are a concern because, unlike most emerging economies, the country imports much more than it exports.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sudeep Jain at sudeep.jain@dowjones.com [ 13-07-12 1216GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120713e87d000t5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
