\par\par \b \uc2 India's cbank sold net $485 mln in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mkt in May\b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2012\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 10 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's (RBI) dollar sales were higher in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot market in May than in April, data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The RBI sold $1.26 billion in May compared with $275 million in the previous month as it tried to rein in the rupee's slide, taking its total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market since the start of September to $22.23 billion.\par \par \uc2 It also rolled over forward dollar contracts by purchasing $778 million in May, the data showed.\par \par \uc2 In the forward dollar market, outstanding dollar sales rose to $10.31 billion in May from $3.45 billion in April, RBI data showed, indicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's preference to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward markets to prevent the rupee liquidity from tightening further in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell about 6 percent in May against the dollar. It settled at 55.4 rupees to a dollar on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Mumbai Treasury Team; Editing by Jijo Jacob)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RBI/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SNI | SNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120713e87a000re\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
