\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Governor: May Announce Bond Buyback Friday\b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2012\par 14:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 6 Jul 2012 08:23 EDT *DJ  RBI's Subbarao: Can't Control Inflation Without Sacrificing Some Short-Term Growth\par \par \uc2 6 Jul 2012 08:24 EDT *DJ  RBI's Subbarao: Low Inflation Essential to Secure Medium-Term Growth\par \par \uc2 6 Jul 2012 08:29 EDT *DJ  RBI's Subbarao: Important to Ensure Inflation Expectations Don't Get Unhinged\par \par \uc2 6 Jul 2012 08:57 EDT *DJ  RBI's Subbarao: Don't Target Any Precise Exchange Rate\par \par \uc2 6 Jul 2012 08:58 EDT *DJ  RBI Only Tries to Smoothen \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Movement - Subbarao\par \par \uc2 6 Jul 2012 08:59 EDT *DJ  RBI's Subbarao: Have to Make Sure \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Intervnetion Is Successful\par \par \uc2 6 Jul 2012 09:00 EDT *DJ  RBI's Subbarao: Have to Be Conscious on Amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 6 Jul 2012 09:10 EDT DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 India Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Head: Low Inflation Essential for Medium-Term Growth\par \par \uc2 By Khushita Vasant\par \par \uc2 KOZHIKODE, India--Bringing down inflation is necessary to secure the economy's medium-term growth prospects though it may lead to some slowdown in the short term, Reserve Bank of India Governor D. Subbarao said Friday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Subbarao, while addressing management students in the southern Indian city of Kozhikode, backed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp rate increases over the past couple of years to control inflation despite rising import cost of fuel and food contributing a large part of the price increases.\par \par \uc2 Inflationary expectations would have firmed up had the RBI not raised rates, Mr. Subbarao said, countering criticism that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was too aggressive in tightening monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The RBI raised its key policy rate 13 times between March 2010 and October 2011 to control inflation. The aggressive monetary tightening has slowed the economy to its weakest growth pace in almost a decade, prompting calls to quickly unwind the rate increases.\par \par \uc2 Subbarao said the RBI may announce a bond-buyback auction later in the day.\par \par \uc2 The RBI has been buying back bonds through auctions every week or two to supplement liquidity in the banking system strained by the government's heavy market borrowing as well as some short-term cash outflows.\par \par \uc2 Write to Khushita Vasant at khushita.vasant@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 06, 2012 09:10 ET (13:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120706e876002ty\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
