\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Head: Low Inflation Essential for Medium-Term Growth\b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2012\par 16:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- RBI may announce bond-buyback auction Friday, Governor Subbarao says\par \par \uc2 -- Buyback announcement could cheer market, say dealers\par \par \uc2 -- RBI conscious on amount of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Subbarao says\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments of RBI governor, market-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  details.)\par \par \uc2 By Khushita Vasant\par \par \uc2 KOZHIKODE, \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 --Bringing down inflation is necessary to secure the economy's medium-term growth prospects though it may lead to some slowdown in the short term, Reserve Bank of India Governor D. Subbarao said Friday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Subbarao, while addressing management students in the southern Indian city of Kozhikode, backed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp rate increases over the past couple of years to control inflation, despite rising import cost of fuel and food contributing a large part of the price increases.\par \par \uc2 Inflationary expectations would have firmed up had the RBI not raised rates, Mr. Subbarao said, countering criticism that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was too aggressive in tightening monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The RBI raised its key policy rate 13 times between March 2010 and October 2011 to control inflation. The aggressive monetary tightening has slowed the economy to its weakest growth pace in almost a decade, prompting calls to quickly unwind the rate increases.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Subbarao said the RBI may announce a bond buyback later in the day.\par \par \uc2 The RBI has been buying back bonds through auctions every week or two to supplement liquidity in the banking system strained by the government's heavy market borrowing as well as some short-term cash outflows.\par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank influences the volume of money by what we call the open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  (buybacks). Today, there must have been an open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... that the Reserve Bank is going to buy bonds" worth 120 billion rupees ($2.17 billion), Mr. Subbarao added.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the comments, which came after markets closed, have raised hopes of a buyback announcement and could lift bond prices Monday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Subbarao also reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of not targeting any particular \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  level and rather \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market only to smoothen excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 He added said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to ensure the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are successful to maintain market confidence, even though it is conscious of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves it has to deal with.\par \par \uc2 The RBI has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent weeks to halt the rupee's fall, but observers worry its ammunition may be limited as India doesn't have very deep \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Subbarao's comments came on a day when the RBI was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the session, selling U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 The move sharply dragged down the greenback from its intraday high of 55.64 rupees. The dollar was trading at 55.40 rupees late in Asia, compared with 54.94 rupees late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has depreciated about 19% against the dollar over the past year, hurt by slowing capital inflows as well as rising imports that have bloated India's current-account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The local unit touched an all-time low of 57.33 to the dollar on June 22.\par \par \uc2 Write to Khushita Vasant at khushita.vasant@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 06, 2012 10:40 ET (14:40 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120706e876003xz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
