\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee falls on oil demand; no sight of RBI\b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2012\par 14:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * No \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen in session\par \par \uc2 * Oil importers dollar demand pressures rupee-dealers\par \par \uc2 * Global risk eyed ahead of EU summit\par \par \uc2 By Subhadip Sircar\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 27 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell on Wednesday, staying near record lows, as oil importers stepped up their dollar purchases at the end of the month, while caution ahead of a European Union Summit sapped demand for risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders did not spot any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the session after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was widely seen as having sold dollars in each of the four previous sessions.\par \par \uc2 Those \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come as the rupee has resumed declines to record lows against the dollar, mirroring declines in May. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its lowest ever at 57.32 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has also failed to gain traction despite measures announced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on India to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including raising the investment limits on government bonds for foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 Edwin Dsouza, senior manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treasury at Essar Services \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said he expected more RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and potentially more measures to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I expect the rupee to trade at 58 to the dollar in the next one month. If that happens, the RBI may come in with more measures," he said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee settled at 57.15/16, compared to Tuesday's close of 57.01/02, and bringing it close to a record closing low of 57.16 hit on June 22.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts were quoted at 57.55, reflecting expectations for further weakness ahead.\par \par \uc2 Global risk sentiments will also play a key role in determining the rupee's fortunes, especially as European Union leaders meet for a two-day summit starting on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The euro steadied against the dollar on Wednesday after hitting a two-week low the previous day, but looked vulnerable to losses as the gathering is not expected to deliver new measures to ease the region's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the United Stock Exchange and the MCX-SX all ended at 57.4650. The total volume was at $3.31 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /CLOSE | ABN | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120630e86r0005a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
