\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Slips; Bonds Lower As Supply Weighs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Khushita Vasant   \par \uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2012\par 15:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     At 1200 GMT \par                          Latest      Change \par    USD/INR                57.15       +0.14 \par    8.79% 2021 Bond        8.36%       +2BP \par    8.15% 2022 Bond        8.12%       +1BP \par    Call Rate              8.10%       -2BP \par    Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    June                   3.3150      +0.255 \par    *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount are midpoints of bid-offer spreads \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI--The Indian rupee slipped against the U.S. dollar in a quiet session Wednesday, as investors across the region kept positions light on the eve of a two-day European Union summit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Weakness in the similarly risk-sensitive euro also rubbed off on the rupee, which clung to a tight trading band.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at INR57.15 late Wednesday in Asia, compared with INR57.01 late Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, stepping in to sell dollars near market closing time as the rupee threatened to breach its intraday low, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The RBI likely sold dollars around INR57.20. This is the fourth consecutive day the dollar has traded above the important psychological level of 57 to the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has declined 21.2% against the dollar over the past 12 months. ICICI Bank Global Markets said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell by 3.1% last week--the biggest weekly drop in nine months.\par \par \uc2 The rupee isn't likely to see much appreciation in the near term as external uncertainties abound, it said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Further, India's move allowing foreigners to invest up to $5 billion more in government bonds Monday to support the rupee will provide little or no immediate respite to the rupee, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "While these measures will help to bring additional debt flows that will lend some support to the rupee in an environment of slowing equity flows, the direction is unlikely to change in the near term," a Macquarie note said. The bank expects weakness in the rupee to persist and pair to trade in the 54-57 band over the next few months.\par \par \uc2 In the government debt market, bonds edged lower as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't announce a bond buyback to support yields and ease tightness in liquidity among banks.\par \par \uc2 The 8.79% 2021 note ended at INR102.77, compared with INR102.85 at Tuesday's close. The tightly held new benchmark 8.15% 2022 bond fell to INR100.17 from INR100.30.\par \par \uc2 The government will sell INR150 billion of bonds at an auction Friday. Earlier Wednesday, the government sold INR150 billion worth of treasury bills.\par \par \uc2 The federal government's large borrowing program of INR5.5 trillion until March has been preventing yields from softening.\par \par \uc2 Even the step allowing greater foreign participation in the bond market hasn't enthused traders. India will next week auction permits to foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said the auction may see only a modest demand, given the restrictions on the maturity of paper a fund can invest in.\par \par \uc2 Write to Khushita Vasant at khushita.vasant@dowjones.com [ 27-06-12 1303GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120627e86r000sc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
