\par\par \b \uc2 Indian bond yields gain; crude prices key\b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2012\par 14:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * 10-yr bond yield ends up 1 bps on Fri and for wk\par \par \uc2 * Slump in global crude prices to support bond prices\par \par \uc2 * More OMOs seen as faltering rupee sparks RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Subhadip Sircar\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark federal bond yield ended marginally higher on Friday because of profit-taking, but hopes of a sustained fall in global crude oil prices and more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond purchases are likely to keep debt prices supported.\par \par \uc2 The slump in oil prices is helping ease some of the concerns about inflationary pressures that were cited by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  as the main reason for keeping interest rates on hold on Monday, a decision that stunned markets.\par \par \uc2 Though yields initially surged after the decision, benchmark 10-year yields have closed up only up 1 basis point for the week, helped as well by expectations the RBI will step up bond purchases via open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The spike in global risk aversion has sent the rupee\par \par \uc2 to a record low against the dollar for a second consecutive session on Friday.\par \par \uc2 That has forced the RBI to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and is thus raising expectations of more OMOs to offset the impact on rupee liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "Signals of weak global demand is pushing down crude, and in turn reining in inflation expectations in India, supporting bonds," said Harish Agarwal, a dealer with First Rand Bank in Mumbai.\par \par \uc2 "Hopes of continuation of OMOs is also helping sentiment."\par \par \uc2 India's 10-year benchmark bond yield rose 1 bp to 8.35 percent on Friday. Total volumes on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's electronic trading platform were at a high 221.20 billion rupees.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the new 8.15 percent 2022 paper ended at 8.08 percent, up 3 basis points.\par \par \uc2 Though the gains for the week were mild, the RBI decision snapped seven consecutive weeks of falling yields, and have put into doubt potential near-term rate cuts, especially after Governor Duvvuri Subbarao followed up with hawkish comments on inflation.\par \par \uc2 The 1-year overnight indexed swap surged 18 basis points for the week, after falling 3 basis points to 7.75 percent on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The longer-end 5-year rate dropped 5 bps to 7.19 percent, ending up 3 bps for the week.\par \par \uc2 Analysts don't expect a rally in bond prices, but at least they expect yields to be capped should the RBI continue to buy bonds via OMOs or in secondary markets.\par \par \uc2 The RBI bought 112.88 billion rupees in government bonds via open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, lower than the notified 120 billion rupees.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll this week showed traders expect 1 trillion rupees in additional OMOs for the rest of the fiscal year ending in March 2013, both to counter \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to inject enough liquidity to allow the government to sell a record 5.3 trillion rupees in bonds.\par \par \uc2 The government sold 150 billion rupees of debt in session, including 70 billion rupees of the most traded 9.15 percent 2024 bond at bullish cutoffs.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-BONDS/ (CLOSE) | ABN | D | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120622e86m000pu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
