\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Indian rupee hits record low; RBI steps in 'mildly'\b0\par\par\uc2 591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2012\par 05:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee falls to record low of 56.55/dollar, ends higher\par \par \uc2 * RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen, but not strong-traders\par \par \uc2 * Rupee vulnerable to global risk, domestic uncertainty\par \par \uc2 (Updates with closing levels)\par \par \uc2 By Subhadip Sircar\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 21 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell to a record low against the dollar on Thursday, as the euro and other risk assets were hit by disappointment about the size of bond purchases announced by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and by weak global economic data.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  made what traders described as a "mild" attempt at defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the session, and some traders said it may have acted again after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly surpassed the previous record low hit on May 31.\par \par \uc2 Just like in May, when the rupee tumbled to a string of record lows, renewed global risk aversion has been the spark for the falls in the rupee, but the decline has been sustained by the deep uncertainty about \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fiscal and economic outlooks.\par \par \uc2 "The RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and policies to mitigate the weakness is not the silver bullet to what really is a structural weakness for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; i.e. the twin deficits," said Nizam Idris, head of Asian fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 Macquarie Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Idris expects the rupee to gradually weaken to 57.5 to the dollar over the next month, though adds a sharp weakening will be prevented as importers and oil companies may have covered most of their hedging needs for the months ahead.\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell at one point to a record low of 56.55 to the dollar, surpassing its previous 56.52 low.\par \par \uc2 However, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered losses on the back of rallying domestic equities to settle at 56.30/31 versus its 56.15/16 close on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Global markets weakened on Thursday after the Fed extended its current bond-buying programme by less than some investors had hoped, while weak factory data from China and a contraction in the euro zone's private sector contributed to the falls.\par \par \uc2 The rupee will remain vulnerable to any flare-ups of global risk aversion, while also subject to domestic challenges.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts closed at 56.71 while the three-month closed at 57.46, implying further losses ahead.\par \par \uc2 The RBI disappointed domestic markets by keeping interest rates on hold on Monday, the same day when Fitch Ratings cut the country's outlook to "negative", becoming the second credit agency to threaten India's investment grade rating.\par \par \uc2 Fitch and S&P have highlighted the growing unease from investors about the lack of visible reform moves by the government despite a toxic macroeconomic cocktail of slowing growth and high inflation.\par \par \uc2 The focus has shifted to the government, which faces a daunting task of reviving faltering economic growth while ensuring its current account and budget deficits do not widen any further.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of India Governor Duvvuri Subbarao this week said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb volatility, blaming the rupee's falls on both global and domestic factors.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 56.4225 on a total volume of $5.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Subhadip Sircar; Editng by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /RUPEE (UPDATE 3) | ABN | M | RBN | SNI | SNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120624e86l00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
