\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee ends flat; RBI may have supported\b0\par\par\uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2012\par 14:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee swings from high of 55.25 to low of 55.91\par \par \uc2 * Split views about whether RBI stepped in to defend rupee\par \par \uc2 * Overnight euro crucial for further rupee direction\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended little changed on Tuesday as dollar sales by exporters and suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped offset the pressures from a weaker euro and from demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from oil firms.\par \par \uc2 Whether the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  generated split views among traders, and any dollars sales were likely to have been mild, they added.\par \par \uc2 The rupee remains well above the record low of 56.52 against the dollar hit on Thursday, and traders say the RBI could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively should the rupee again fall below 56 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Global risk factors will remain key in the near-term, especially ahead of a meeting of G7 finance ministers that is expected to address the growing euro zone debt woes.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has also been hit by waning confidence on India's economic outlook, although a majority of economists polled by Reuters now predict at least a 25 basis points cut at its June 18 meeting.\par \par \uc2 "Demand for dollars is likely to stay high amid uncertainty in Spain and ahead of the Greece elections, keeping pressure on the rupee," said Pramod Patil, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with \uc2 United Overseas Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupee fell to an intra-day low of 55.91 before closing at 55.64/65 as per the SBI closing rate, not much changed from its 55.66/67 close on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had started the day with gains on the back of some revival in risk-taking globally, p ushing the rupee at one point to a one-week high of 55.25 per dollar in early trade.\par \par \uc2 However, that was later offset as oil companies, the largest buyers of dollars in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, stepped up purchases of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro also skidded, pressuring the rupee, on ongoing concerns over whether Spain can restore its banks to health.\par \par \uc2 Whether the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains in doubt, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars frequently in both spot and forward markets last month.\par \par \uc2 "There were state-run banks on offer starting 55.87 levels, not sure whether it was for the RBI, but could very well be," a senior dealer with a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 Offshore traders expect further weakness in the rupee. The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts were quoted at 56.01, while the three-month was at 56.73.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 55.93 on a total volume of $3.7 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (CLOSE) | ABN | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120608e865000qt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
