\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Indian rupee falls; some see bottom\b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2012\par 05:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee falls vs dollar for first session in three\par \par \uc2 * RBI watched for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should rupee fall past 56\par \par \uc2 * RBI signals room to cut interest rates to boost growth\par \par \uc2 (Updates quote, adds details, closing levels)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 4 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee weakened for the first day in three against the dollar, retreating from a one-week high earlier, as oil importers stepped in to buy the U.S. unit, while waning greenback sales by corporates and exporters in late trade also hurt.\par \par \uc2 Despite Monday's fall, the rupee remains well above the record low of 56.52 against the dollar hit on Thursday, indicating a near-term bottom after a rough last month.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was dented badly by a mix of global risk aversion and concerns about India's economic and fiscal challenges in May.\par \par \uc2 Global risk factors will continue to be important, and traders say the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively should the rupee again fall below 56 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could also cut interest rates as early as this month, which may contribute to a recovery in the rupee by helping boost confidence in the sagging economy, one of the key factors behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide.\par \par \uc2 "Rupee could gain towards 55 per dollar if oil companies refrain from buying in the market, while the topside may be capped at 56 on expectations of RBI coming in," said Uday Bhatt, senior manager \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing with state-run \uc2 UCO Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible unit closed at 55.66/67 per dollar as per SBI, falling from its 55.54/55 close on Friday and the one-week high at 55.26 hit earlier in the session.\par \par \uc2 The rupee had started the session with gains, as a mid-sized infrastructure company was spotted selling dollars for a third straight session.\par \par \uc2 One trader said the company had $1 billion worth of inflows, of which $650 million had hit the market on Thursday and Friday.\par \par \uc2 In the near-term, the rupee could also benefit as demand for dollars from oil importers typically wanes as the beginning of the month, although they do step in to take advantage of levels.\par \par \uc2 "The rupee may start stronger tomorrow, and I expect oil firms to come in again, so broadly see the rupee in a 55.20-55.70 band," said Hari Chandramgathan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with Federal Bank.\par \par \uc2 RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be the most important factor in the near-term, however. After frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both spot and forward markets last month, the RBI is believed to have stayed mostly in the sidelines in recent days.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the rupee would need increased confidence in the economy to sustain gains, either in the form of fiscal consolidation steps from the government, or potentially easier monetary policy from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A deputy governor of the RBI said on Monday falling global oil prices as well as declining core inflation and growth in India give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more room to adjust interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Still, offshore traders expect further weakness in the rupee. The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were quoted at 56.01, while the three-month was at 56.73.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most-traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange all ended around 55.73 on a total volume of $4.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Rafael Nam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA/RUPEE (UPDATE 2) | ABN | M | RBN | SNI | SNS | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120607e8640004k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
