\par\par \b \uc2 Reserve Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Likely  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Friday - Traders\b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2012\par 06:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen in the market again Friday, stepping in as the rupee continued to trade near the key psychological low of 56 for a third straight session, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  likely started selling dollars when the greenback was at INR55.92, four dealers told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 After the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar fell to the day's low of INR55.74 after hitting a high of INR56.08.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at INR55.65 last in Asia Thursday, compared with a fresh all-time high of INR56.37 earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 An RBI spokeswoman wasn't immediately available for comment.\par \par \uc2 The RBI doesn't say whether it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has a stated policy of getting into the market only to limit volatility. It is suspected of having been in the market several times in recent days.\par \par \uc2 -By Khushita Vasant & Sourav Mishra, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6122; khushita.vasant@dowjones.com [ 25-05-12 0430GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020120525e85p00009\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\